==== Serial ====
The signals of the built-in UART lines can be found on the expansion connector. The full pinout of the expansion connector can be found in the user guide of the device.

| <code>
Serial pinout:
           |                   |                   |    |     SHIELD
           |                   |        CPU        |    |_____________
           |                   |___________________|                  
 7: 3.3V   |                                                          
41: GND    |                                                          
45: TX     |       49         _____________________________         1 
47: RX     |        o o o o o|o o o o o o o o o o o o o o o|o o o o o
           |        o o o o o|o o o o o o o o o o o o o o o|o o o o o
           |       50         -----------------------------         2
           |__________________________________________________________
</code> |

The UART lines are operating at TTL voltage levels, so if you want to connect it to your PC, you need a TTL-to-RS232 level shifter. See the [[http://nuwiki.openwrt.org/oldwiki/openwrtdocs/customizing/hardware/serial_console|Serial Console]] article for more informations.

